{
  "message": "Good news first: the local check found no failures, and every component and flow is still in place. The remaining blockers are missing build code, not design mistakes. The only one we can fix in the design is \"Approved knowledge\": it's a private Cloud Storage bucket, which matches a supported contract, so I've proposed marking it as one. Staff sign-in, the console, the orchestrator, retrieval and the CRM adapter all need new product code before they can be built. Who should be allowed to upload, update and delete the approved articles in that bucket, for example a named knowledge-team service account?",
  "phase": "Architecture Review",
  "proposal": {
    "baseRevision": 2,
    "title": "Bind Approved knowledge to the GCP private-object-storage contract",
    "body": "This change only sets implementation=private-object-storage on the existing Cloud Storage bucket (kbstore). No components, IDs, flows or requirements are removed. The Vertex AI Search indexing link (e5) and the other Cloud Run, IAP and Pub/Sub components remain open implementation gaps that need product engineering. No uploader access is added until the user names a principal. Region, project and identities are not verified. Rerun emulation on the new artifact.",
